@page "/"

<PageTitle>AT · Research Atlas</PageTitle>
@using AT.App.Services
@inject ValidationDataService ValidationDataService

<div>
    <MudImage Src="/images/at-image1_web_small.jpg" Height="150" ObjectFit="ObjectFit.Cover" style="width:100%"/>
</div>

<div class="hero">
    <div class="hero-kicker">Research Atlas · @AtlasDataService.VersionLabel</div>
    <div class="hero-title">The Actualization Theory</div>
    <div class="hero-subtitle">A Reconstruction of Physics from Difference, Actualization and Spectrum</div>
    <div class="hero-tagline">A theory book and validation atlas for the AT program.</div>
</div>

<div class="page-section mt-4">
    <h2 class="section-heading">Quantum gravity highlight</h2>
    <MudCard Elevation="1" Class="theory-card">
        <MudCardContent>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Class="muted">
                After V2.1 the theory reduces to <strong>one object</strong>: the count density
                <strong>ρ</strong> generated by Actualization
                (Difference → Distinguishability → event → spectrum → complex state → ρ, S_001).
                ρ has two derived faces — <strong>information</strong>
                (I = KL(ρ‖uniform) = 0.7513 nats, feeding ΩΛ = 0.6839) and
                <strong>geometry</strong> (g = ρ^(2/d)η, the unique conformal metric preserving
                the count, √(−g) = ρ ⟹ k = 2/d, feeding gravity).
            </MudText>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Class="muted mt-2">
                Measurement is the readout face: one actualization event reads both quadratures
                of one mode (M_001), gains log₂95 bits, and conserves information by
                redistribution. The deepest remaining boundary is the discreteness of the
                actualization tick (QG_011), from which finite events and observable finiteness
                follow.
            </MudText>
        </MudCardContent>
    </MudCard>
</div>

<div class="page-section mt-4">
    <h2 class="section-heading">Why AT?</h2>
    <div class="why-grid">
        @foreach (var q in AtlasDataService.WhyQuestions)
        {
            <div class="why-tile"><span class="q">@q</span></div>
        }
    </div>
    <p class="mt-2">
        AT investigates whether observable physics can emerge from a smaller primitive foundation.
        <a href="/story">Read the full story &rarr;</a>
    </p>
</div>

<div class="page-section">
    <h2 class="section-heading">Recent Findings</h2>
    <p class="muted">The latest AT-QG phases (auto-updated from the coverage JSON).</p>
    @if (_coverage is not null && _coverage.RecentFindings.Count > 0)
    {
        <MudGrid Spacing="3">
            @foreach (var f in _coverage.RecentFindings)
            {
                <MudItem xs="12" sm="6" lg="4">
                    <MudCard Elevation="1" Class="theory-card h-100">
                        <MudCardContent>
                            <MudText Typo="Typo.caption" Class="text-uppercase fw-bold muted">@(f.PhaseLabel ?? $"AT-QG {(int)f.Phase}") · @f.Classification</MudText>
                            <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle1" Class="fw-bold mt-1">@f.Title</MudText>
                            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Class="muted mt-2">
                                @f.Summary
                            </MudText>
                            <div class="mt-3">
                                <span class="badge @BadgeClassFor(f.Validation)">@f.Validation</span>
                                <span class="badge badge-neutral">@f.Domain</span>
                            </div>
                            <MudButton Variant="Variant.Text" Color="Color.Primary" Href="@f.ReportUrl"
                                       Target="_blank" Rel="noopener" Class="mt-2 px-0" Size="Size.Small">
                                Report <i class="bi bi-box-arrow-up-right"></i>
                            </MudButton>
                        </MudCardContent>
                    </MudCard>
                </MudItem>
            }
        </MudGrid>
    }
    else
    {
        <MudProgressCircular Indeterminate="true" Size="Size.Small" />
    }
</div>

<div class="page-section">
    <h2 class="section-heading">Research Journey</h2>
    <div class="story-flow">
        @for (int i = 0; i < AtlasDataService.StoryChapters.Count; i++)
        {
            <span class="@($"badge tone-{AtlasDataService.StoryChapters[i].Tone}")"><i class="@($"bi {AtlasDataService.StoryChapters[i].Icon}")"></i>&nbsp;@AtlasDataService.StoryChapters[i].Era</span>
            @if (i < AtlasDataService.StoryChapters.Count - 1)
            {
                <span class="chain-arrow">&darr;</span>
            }
        }
    </div>
    <p class="muted mt-2">TRM &rarr; Problems Found &rarr; ResearchX &rarr; Structure/Content Split &rarr; Hostile Reviews &rarr; AT v1.0 &rarr; D96 Program &rarr; V2.0 &rarr; V2.1 &rarr; V2.2&nbsp;(<a href="/research-journey">full journey</a>).</p>
</div>

<div class="page-section">
    <h2 class="section-heading">From TRM to AT</h2>
    <MudCard Elevation="1" Class="theory-card">
        <MudCardContent>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Class="muted">
                AT's predecessor, the Temporal Resonance Model, assembled striking pieces but carried zero
                candidate physics. The legacy audit absorbed three modules, rejected two, and kept three as
                candidate mathematics. AT re-derived the surviving structure from the primitives
                {Difference, η} plus the observable-sector inputs — the Z2-paired complex sector, three
                octave families, and the SU(2) weak sector (R_001).
            </MudText>
        </MudCardContent>
    </MudCard>
</div>

<div class="page-section">
    <h2 class="section-heading">Key Discoveries</h2>
    <MudGrid Spacing="3">
        @foreach (var d in AtlasDataService.KeyDiscoveries)
        {
            <MudItem xs="12" sm="6" lg="4">
                <TheoryCard Title="@d.Title">
                    <ClassificationBadge Kind="@d.Kind" />
                    <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Class="muted mt-2">@d.Description</MudText>
                </TheoryCard>
            </MudItem>
        }
    </MudGrid>
</div>

<div class="page-section">
    <h2 class="section-heading">Prediction Status</h2>
    <MudCard Elevation="1" Class="theory-card">
        <MudCardContent>
            @if (_outcomes is null)
            {
                <MudProgressCircular Indeterminate="true" Size="Size.Small" />
            }
            else
            {
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Class="muted">
                    The three pre-registered predictions (P1 106 GeV, P2 0νββ 2.02 meV, P3 sector-ladder)
                    are immutable. Current states:
                    <span class="status-chip status-pending">P1 PENDING</span>
                    <span class="status-chip status-pending">P2 PENDING</span>
                    <span class="status-chip status-partial">P3 SUPPORTED</span>
                    &nbsp;(151.98 rung = ~152 GeV excess)
                </MudText>
                <MudButton Variant="Variant.Outlined" Color="Color.Primary" Href="/validation/prediction-status" Class="mt-2">
                    Prediction status
                </MudButton>
            }
        </MudCardContent>
    </MudCard>
</div>

<div class="page-section">
    <div class="mb-2">
        <span class="badge badge-derived">DERIVED</span>
        <span class="badge badge-emergent">EMERGENT</span>
        <span class="badge badge-boundary">BOUNDARY</span>
        <span class="muted">&mdash; the classification used by the ResearchY audits throughout this atlas.</span>
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    private PhysicsCoverageFile? _coverage;
    private PredictionOutcomeFile? _outcomes;

    /// <summary>Maps a phase validation status to a badge CSS class.</summary>
    private static string BadgeClassFor(string validation)
        => validation switch
        {
            "tested" => "badge-derived",
            "partial" => "badge-partial",
            "audit" => "badge-compatible",
            _ => "badge-neutral",
        };

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        _coverage = await ValidationDataService.GetCoverageAsync();
        _outcomes = await ValidationDataService.GetOutcomesAsync();
    }
}
